{"skill":{"slug":"skill-creator","displayName":"Skill Creator"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769522677376,"changelog":"Initial release of skill-creator, a comprehensive guide for designing modular skills to extend Claude’s capabilities.\n\n- Introduces principles for creating effective, concise, and domain-specific skills.\n- Explains modular structure: required SKILL.md and optional scripts, references, and assets folders.\n- Outlines guidelines for what to include (and exclude) in a skill package.\n- Details progressive disclosure design for efficient context management.\n- Provides reference patterns for organizing content and bundling resources.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"LICENSE.txt","size":11357,"sha256":"58d1e17ffe5109a7ae296caafcadfdbe6a7d176f0bc4ab01e12a689b0499d8bd","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":17837,"sha256":"b2e3d83f60425c2d0b9d4162efb8f9aa322b45843497340f2289f42be422801c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/output-patterns.md","size":1813,"sha256":"d6027800b9d8c26589edba85b42901a41ac36d753b4e9cebc7f4cbb03cdcf0a4","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/workflows.md","size":818,"sha256":"ef4846877d5dab47511a01a6cf31476ad64f5bc5945635459295794575338980","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/init_skill.py","size":10863,"sha256":"0bba250b94caa4cb2b28b15dad26fdcf371aeda4c9797b8120e55c2e33e0c73c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/package_skill.py","size":3288,"sha256":"b31fbcb3e362d5c5308e99255ff8e83cde3a513e0636953964a648494ca10931","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/quick_validate.py","size":3523,"sha256":"381ab2d3d1fd5ec32371016413063eff99d0d48c415747085c61517e967dbb87","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1852,"sha256":"fdb9815e693a1e3514f450ec40b0acbf00556abf86939e9ee05420e350a84f5e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022038599,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"61d012fc000bb6baafa4ca972ee8e2c262840a6ae2c2dfa665ef2914a944d693","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/61d012fc000bb6baafa4ca972ee8e2c262840a6ae2c2dfa665ef2914a944d693","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: skill-creator\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious primarily due to the `scripts/init_skill.py` file. This script creates a new skill directory and, as part of its templating process, generates an `example.py` file within the `scripts/` subdirectory, setting its permissions to `0o755` (executable). While the content of the generated `example.py` is a benign placeholder, the capability to create executable files in a user-specified path, even for templating, represents a significant security risk if the script's inputs were controlled by a malicious actor or if the template itself were altered. The `SKILL.md` and other files are instructional and do not contain malicious prompt injection or other harmful behaviors.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160128702},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":93,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789022038599},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent skill-authoring helper, but its packaging script can accidentally include sensitive local files through symlinks.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The packaging helper recursively archives local files and follows symlinks, which can copy readable files outside the intended skill directory into the .skill archive; the initializer also lacks skill-name containment checks and can create a new directory tree outside the requested base path.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No separate install hook, dependency installer, network fetch, or automatic execution mechanism was found in the inspected artifact files.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are broad but centered on creating or updating skills; scanner self-modification concerns appear to refer to editing target skills, not hidden modification of this installed skill.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"When user-run, the initializer creates files and an executable example script, but there is no evidence of background persistence, privilege escalation, credential use, or automatic execution.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is skill creation guidance, and the bundled init, validation, reference, and packaging helpers are mostly aligned with that workflow.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing or using in automated workflows. Use it only on trusted skill directories, avoid packaging directories that may contain symlinks, and run its helper scripts in a sandbox or low-privilege workspace until the symlink and path-containment issues are fixed.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the scripts for initialization, validation, and packaging are explicitly described in SKILL.md as part of the skill creation process, so they are not unrelated hidden behavior.\n[RA1] expected: Downgraded: references to writing or updating SKILL.md are instructions for authoring target skills and generated templates, not evidence that the installed skill modifies itself at runtime.\n[LP3] unexpected: Partially accepted as a documentation gap: the frontmatter does not declare allowed tools, though the runtime behavior is disclosed in the body and scripts.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded: the trigger phrase is broad, but it is still limited to users creating or updating skills and the body advises including specific trigger contexts in new skills.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: scripts/package_skill.py uses rglob(), Path.is_file(), and ZipFile.write() without rejecting symlinks or checking resolved-path containment, so packaging an untrusted skill directory can disclose local readable files into the archive.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted with lower impact than the symlink issue: scripts/init_skill.py documents restrictive skill-name rules but does not enforce them before joining paths, allowing creation of a new template directory outside the requested output directory if invoked with traversal or absolute-name input.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022038599}}}}}